No introduced actionable security findings. Close payload exposes only an optional integer code, never untrusted close reason or URL credentials. Disconnect occurs before emitting the error; identity checks suppress abandoned/intentional channel closures. Factory-owned client disposal disconnects open/pending connections, while direct override ownership is documented. Pinning, release-wss policy, redirect policy and existing URL redaction remain unchanged and tested. No auth/session persistence, transport selection or dependencies changed.
Public evidence contains local test-server endpoints and redacted synthetic query/userinfo fixtures; no apparent live credentials, authorization bearer, private key or live-key signature found. No tracked edits or GitHub mutations. No device/backend deployment assurance asserted.
